KZ3 patch 1166: the runtime's frameless host setjmp/longjmp on MinGW x64 no longer go through the CRT.
Port of patch 7066 of a sibling PS3 port by the same maintainer (identical change); credit goes to that patch.

Public issue #58 (exit 0xC0000409 under 1 s, right after the first SPURS workload starts) is probably this: on real
Windows with Control Flow Guard active, ucrtbase's longjmp calls __except_validate_jump_buffer, which __fastfail(13)s
when Frame == 0 (seen in a minidump of that sibling port; Wine has no CFG). The runtime's frameless jumps write Frame = 0
on purpose (_setjmp(buf, NULL): KZ3 patch 1099 SPU halt/drain, 1116 PPU guest setjmp host frames; no RtlUnwindEx over
lifted frames). ASSUMPTION: #58 has no reporter dump, so the cause is not confirmed.

runtime/platform/host_jmp_win64.h: rc_host_setjmp / rc_host_longjmp, naked ms_abi functions saving and restoring the
Win64 callee-saved state, no validation and no unwind. Used by ppu_setjmp.h (PPU_SJ_HOST_*), spu_context.h
(SPU_SETJMP/SPU_LONGJMP), and through them spu_channels.c and spu_drain.c, on MinGW x64 only; other hosts unchanged.
Every setjmp/longjmp pair on that host uses the new pair (no CRT/new mix). Host test: tools/spu/test_host_jmp_win64.sh.
Upstream candidate (every ps3recomp title built with MinGW on Windows).

